From 8961f4c5410f5459487af7fc110858100c0cf26d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Klemm <github@tklemm.eu>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:06:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep Pathname::SEPARATOR_PAT as a deprecated constant

Bundler before 4.0.12 evaluates /\A#{Pathname::SEPARATOR_PAT}/o in
Bundler::Source::Path#generate_bin, which runs for every gem installed
from a path or git source, including the gem of a Gemfile that says
`gemspec`.  Bundler switches to the version named in BUNDLED WITH, so
`bundle install` with a lockfile written by Bundler 2.x or 4.0.0 to
4.0.11 fails on master with "uninitialized constant
Pathname::SEPARATOR_PAT" since 4e243c709e made the constant private and
a5996718f3 removed it.  Bundler itself no longer uses it (ruby/rubygems
PR 9529, released in 4.0.12).

Define it again with the value it had in 4.0 and deprecate it, so such
lockfiles keep installing and code that still reads it warns under
-W:deprecated.
---
 pathname_builtin.rb            | 4 ++++
 test/pathname/test_pathname.rb | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pathname_builtin.rb b/pathname_builtin.rb
index 4cabfb30c4..b397a0b313 100644
--- a/pathname_builtin.rb
+++ b/pathname_builtin.rb
@@ -363,6 +363,10 @@ class Pathname
 
   # :stopdoc:
 
+  # Read by Bundler before 4.0.12, which older lockfiles still install.
+  SEPARATOR_PAT = File::ALT_SEPARATOR ? /[#{Regexp.quote(File::ALT_SEPARATOR + File::SEPARATOR)}]/ : /#{Regexp.quote(File::SEPARATOR)}/
+  deprecate_constant :SEPARATOR_PAT
+
   attr_reader :path
   protected :path
 
diff --git a/test/pathname/test_pathname.rb b/test/pathname/test_pathname.rb
index 2c7ec3f800..5ffdf69702 100644
--- a/test/pathname/test_pathname.rb
+++ b/test/pathname/test_pathname.rb
@@ -195,6 +195,12 @@ def del_trailing_separator(path)
     defassert(:del_trailing_separator, "\225".dup.force_encoding("cp437"), "\225\\\\".dup.force_encoding("cp437"))
   end
 
+  def test_separator_pat
+    assert_deprecated_warning(/SEPARATOR_PAT/) do
+      assert_match(/\A#{Pathname::SEPARATOR_PAT}/, "/usr")
+    end
+  end
+
   def test_plus
     assert_kind_of(Pathname, Pathname("a") + Pathname("b"))
   end
-- 
